449 - Never Part Again
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 449
Topic: Early Advent - 

Verse 1:
[Bb7/Ab]There is a land of pure delight,
[Bb7/F]Where bliss eternal reigns,
[Eb]Infinite day excludes the night
[Eb/Bb]And pleasures banish pain.

Refrain:
[Bb7]We're trav'ling to [Eb]Immanuel's land,
[Eb]We soon shall hear the trumpet sound,
[Eb]And soon we shall with Jesus reign,
[Eb]And never, never part again.
[Eb]What! Never part again? [Bb7/F]No, never part again,
[Eb]What! Never part again? No, never part again,
[Ab]And soon we shall with Jesus reign,
[Bb]And never, never part again.

Verse 2:
[Bb7/Ab]There everlasting spring abides,
[Bb7/F]And never with'ring flowers,
[Eb]And but a little space divides
[Eb/Bb]This heav'nly land from ours.

Verse 3:
[Bb7/Ab]Could we but stand where Moses stood,
[Bb7/F]And view the landscape o'er,
[Eb]Not all this world's pretended good
[Eb/Bb]Could ever charm us more.
